CREATED:20221119T180325Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><span>On<span>&nbsp\;</span></span><b><b>Saturday\, 
 December 3 at 5pm</b></b><span><span>&nbsp\;</span>we will host a Christmas
  Jazz Concert.&nbsp\; Tickets are $25 per person or $15 for seniors/student
 s.&nbsp\;</span><br><br><span>To get tickets: visit our<span>&nbsp\;</span>
 </span><a href="https://www.eservicepayments.com/cgi-bin/Vanco_ver3.vps?app
 ver3=Fi1giPL8kwX_Oe1AO50jRiZqwosAhO_mWDnSRn9t9d_HO3iVYxvvxhHjRfLOeq662EvVVA
 EjqawDomKT1pboucAFyZL5AUEYLjKz18ZTy3c=">e-payment page</a><span>&nbsp\; OR 
 Venmo<span>&nbsp\;</span></span><b><b>Holy Spirit Verona @Jerry-Racioppi-2<
 span>&nbsp\;</span></b></b><span>[</span><b><b><font>6663</font></b></b><sp
 an>] (put "concert" in comments) OR at the door.&nbsp\;</span><br><br><span
 >Light refreshments and beverages will be available following the concert.&
 nbsp\;</span><br><br><span>Our Cantor Ema Mitrović will be the vocalist\, o
 n drums will be Tim Horner\, on piano Oscar Perez and on bass Bill Moring.​
 </span></html-blob><br><html-blob><span>&nbsp\;</span></html-blob><br><html
 -blob><span></span><p><strong><span>Ema Mitrović&nbsp\;</span></strong><spa
 n>- Award winning andcritically acclaimed operatic mezzo-soprano/vocalist\,
  Ema Mitrović\, isdescribed: “out of the ensemble\, I found Ema Mitrovic..
 .to be the standout”(Opera Manhattan\, Suor Angelica ’12) and "Her rich mez
 zo is purepleasure..” (Hudson Opera Theatre\, Lucia di Lammermoor ’18). Ms.
  Mitrovićperforms as an ambassador of music across different genres\, havi
 ng performed 19operatic roles thus far\, a number of solo recitals\, and ha
 s enjoyed being astrong cross-over jazz singer\, performing along New York 
 City’s finestmusicians\, including Tim Horner\, Joe Locke\, Ted Rosenthal\,
  and Jim Ridl\, to namea few. She's been on stage at Carnegie Hall\, Lincol
 n Center\, and New YorkCity's renowned jazz venues Birdland\, The Kitano\, 
 and Smalls. Often\, sheperforms programs that include both classical and st
 andard jazz repertoire toconnect to her audience. This season\, despite str
 ains from the Covid-19pandemic\, Ema was grateful to perform in recital at 
 Brooklyn’s Soapbox Galleryand Nyack’s Maureen’s Jazz Cellar\, as Annina (La
  Traviata) with The LighthouseOpera Company\, and recording with the New Je
 rsey Youth Symphony ChamberEnsemble in a newly commissioned piece\, “La Fro
 ntera” by Raul Abbad. Later thisseason\, Ema will return to New York’s The 
 Lighthouse Opera Company in Mozart'sDie Zauberflöte (Dritte Dame) as well a
 s make a role/company debut with BronxOpera Company in its production of Th
 e Bartered Bride (Háta). As passionate aperformer\, Ema is equally as passi
 onate in teaching\, having done so for 7+years. During the Covid 19 quarant
 ine\, Ema has been proud to keep a full studioremotely (on Zoom\, Skype\, F
 aceTime\, etc) of roughly 30+ voice and pianostudents\, at both the non-pro
 fit The Wharton Institute for the Performing Artsand privately owned Elefan
 te Music\, among her own. Ms. Mitrović is a proudfirst generation Croatian
 -American\, born and raised in New Jersey. Shecontinues to study vocal tech
 nique with Maestro Braeden Harris.</span></p><p><strong><span>Tim Horner&nb
 sp\;</span></strong><span>-&nbsp\;born 1956 inRoanoke Va. began playing dru
 ms and violin at the age of 10 . He continued hismusic endeavors through hi
 gh school always keeping his eyes on his goal ofbeing a professional musici
 an \, most notably to play jazz music.&nbsp\;In 1974after graduating from P
 atrick Henry High School in Roanoke Va. he moved toBoston to attend Berklee
  College of Music which he graduated in 1979 with aBachelors degree in Jazz
  Performance. During those years he played and recordedaround the Boston ar
 ea with Al Cohn\, Buddy Defranco\, Miroslav Vitous\, SalNistico\, Herb Pomo
 eroy\, various Berklee ensembles and many local Bostonmusicians. He also to
 ok a year of from school and traveled with The TommyDorsey Orch.&nbsp\;Afte
 r moving to NYC in 1980\, he has been a strong voice ofthe NYC jazz scene b
 oth playing\, recording and traveling extensively around theworld. He has w
 orked with and recorded on over 200 recordings with artistsincluding Ted Na
 sh\, Maria Schneider\, Houston Person\, Joe Locke\, Roseanna Vitro\,Ann Ham
 pton Calloway\, BIll Cunliffe\, Ted Rosenthal and many more. In the lastfew
  years Tim has recorded 3 CD projects of his own which 2 of them include al
 lof his own compositions and arrangements. In the last 18 years Tim has bee
 n onthe faculty of New Jersey City University as their jazz drum instructor
  as wellas leading ensembles.&nbsp\;Tim has also been a 4 time representati
 ve for theU.S. State Department working for the Jazz Ambassador program and
  working inconjunction with The Kennedy Center and Lincoln Center. These to
 urs took him ontours concertizing as well as teaching in South America\, Ea
 stern Europe and theBalkans\, Turkey\, Cypress\, Asia\, Russia\, Kazakhstan
  and Kyrgystan.</span></p><p><strong><span>Oscar Perez</span></strong><span
 >&nbsp\;- Pleasesee&nbsp\;</span><span><a href="https://www.oscarperezmusic
 .com/about"><span>Oscar's website</span></a></span><span>.</span></p><p><st
 rong><span>Bill Moring</span></strong><span>&nbsp\;- BassistBill Moring is 
 a versatile jazz artist whose scope includes playing in the bigbands of leg
 ends Count Basie and Woody Herman\, jammin' jazz/funk and beyondwith the Da
 ve Stryker/Steve Slagle quartet or stretching harmonic and rhythmicboundari
 es with John Hart and Chris Potter. He attended Indiana StateUniversity whi
 le also playing in cellist Hank Roberts group\, gigging aroundIndianapolis 
 and Cincinnati and studying with local pianists Claude Sifferlenand Steve A
 llee. In 1980 he began working with John Von Ohlen's big band\,playing at t
 he Jazz Kitchen in Indianapolis\, recording a live record that wasGrammy no
 minated. &nbsp\;He also played locally with Dizzy Gillespie\, SlideHampton\
 , and Cal Collins. After moving to New York City in 1984\, Bill workedwith 
 drummer Mel Lewis. He toured with Woody Herman's Thundering Herd in 1985and
  received a National Endowment for the Arts Grant to study with Rufus Reidi
 n 1986. He continued his studies with the legendary Homer Mensch. In 1987-8
 8\,Bill toured with the Count Basie Orchestra. Some other big band experien
 cesinclude the Village Vanguard Orchestra\, the Toshiko Akiyoshi/Lew Tabaki
 n JazzOrchestra\, and the Bill Mobley Jazz Orchestra. He has played with re
 nowned singerssuch as Joe Williams\, Mel Tormé and Susannah McCorkle\, and 
 with jazz legendsFrank Foster\, Al Cohn\, Clark Terry\, Mickey Roker\, Tomm
 y Flanagan\, Junior Cook\,Roland Hanna and Ray Barretto. He has also perfor
 med and/or recorded with manycontemporary artists including John Abercrombi
 e\, Gary Bartz\, Manolo Badrena\,Larry Coryell\, Vic Juris\, Dave Kikoski\,
  Billy Hart\, John Hart\, Eddie Henderson\,Joe Locke\, Mulgrew Miller\, Chr
 is Potter\, Dom Salvador\, Dave Stryker\, and JamesWilliams.</span></p>&nbs
 p\; <span><br></span></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T115350Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Christmas Jazz Concert & Reception
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
