CREATED:20250423T161203Z
DESCRIPTION:<span>We will celebrate <b><span>The Feast of Julian Norwich</s
 pan></b> on <b><span>Sunday\, May 11 </span></b>(even though her actual fea
 st day is May 8). This fifteenth century <b><span>Mystic and Theologian</sp
 an></b> lived in an anchorage in Norwich England during the bubonic plaque 
 and has much to teach us today.  Here are the </span><span><a href="https:/
 /www.episcopalchurch.org/lectionary/julian-of-norwich/" target="_blank"><sp
 an>scripture readings</span></a></span><span> for her Feast Day and some </
 span><span><a href="https://www.episcopalchurch.org/glossary/julian-of-norw
 ich/" target="_blank"><span>information</span></a></span><span> about her l
 ife.  Join us as we hear of her "Revelations" and gifts to the world.  <i><
 b><span>#mothersday2025</span></b></i></span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T115427Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FEAST OF JULIAN OF NORWICH
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
