UID:31tnnnpg682iit2jqfan5tuf5j@google.com
CREATED:20231030T204505Z
DESCRIPTION:<span>On<span> </span></span><b><b>Sunday\, December 10 at 4pm<
 /b></b><span><span> </span>we will host a Christmas Jazz Concert. Tickets a
 re $25 per person or $15 for students. </span><br><br><span>To get tickets:
  visit our<span> </span></span><a href="https://www.eservicepayments.com/cg
 i-bin/Vanco_ver3.vps?appver3=Fi1giPL8kwX_Oe1AO50jRiZqwosAhO_mWDnSRn9t9d_HO3
 iVYxvvxhHjRfLOeq662EvVVAEjqawDomKT1pboucAFyZL5AUEYLjKz18ZTy3c=">e-payment p
 age</a><span>  OR Venmo<span> </span></span><b><b>Holy Spirit Verona @Jerry
 -Racioppi-2<span> </span></b></b><span>[</span><b><b><font>6663</font></b><
 /b><span>] (put "concert" in comments) OR at the door. </span><br><br><span
 >Light refreshments and beverages will be available following the concert. 
 </span><br><br><span>Our Music Director\, <b>Ema Mitrović</b> will be the v
 ocalist\, on drums will be <b>Tim Horner</b>\, on piano <b>Joshua Richman <
 /b>and on bass <b>Anthony Perez</b>.​</span><br><u></u><span> </span><u></u
 ><br><u></u><span></span><p><b><span>Ema Mitrović </span></b><span>- Award 
 winning and critically acclaimed operatic mezzo-soprano/vocalist\, Ema Mitr
 ović\, is described: “out of the ensemble\, I found Ema Mitrovi</span><spa
 n><span>ć</span></span><span>...to be the standout”(Opera Manhattan\, Suor
  Angelica ’12) and "Her rich mezzo is pure pleasure..” (Hudson Opera Theatr
 e\, Lucia di Lammermoor ’18). Ms. Mitrović performs as an ambassador of mu
 sic across different genres\, having performed 19operatic roles thus far\, 
 a number of solo recitals\, and has enjoyed being a strong cross-over jazz 
 singer\, performing along New York City’s finest musicians\, including Tim 
 Horner\, Joe Locke\, Ted Rosenthal\, and Jim Ridl\, to name a few. She's be
 en on stage at Carnegie Hall\, Lincoln Center\, and New YorkCity's renowned
  jazz venues Birdland\, The Kitano\, and Smalls. Often\, she performs progr
 ams that include both classical and standard jazz repertoire to connect to 
 her audience. This season\, despite strains from the Covid-19 pandemic\, Em
 a was grateful to perform in recital at Brooklyn’s Soapbox Gallery and Nyac
 k’s Maureen’s Jazz Cellar\, as Annina (La Traviata) with The Lighthouse Ope
 ra Company\, and recording with the New Jersey Youth Symphony Chamber Ensem
 ble in a newly commissioned piece\, “La Frontera” by Raul Abbad. Later this
  season\, Ema will return to New York’s The Lighthouse Opera Company in Moz
 art's Die Zauberflöte (Dritte Dame) as well as make a role/company debut wi
 th Bronx Opera Company in its production of The Bartered Bride (Háta). As p
 assionate a performer\, Ema is equally as passionate in teaching\, having d
 one so for 7+years. During the Covid 19 quarantine\, Ema has been proud to 
 keep a full studio remotely (on Zoom\, Skype\, FaceTime\, etc) of roughly 3
 0+ voice and piano students\, at both the non-profit The Wharton Institute 
 for the Performing Arts and privately owned Elefante Music\, among her own.
  Ms. Mitrović is a proud first generation Croatian-American\, born and rai
 sed in New Jersey. She continues to study vocal technique with Maestro Brae
 den Harris.</span></p><p><b><span>Tim Horner </span></b><span>- born 1956 i
 n Roanoke Va. began playing drums and violin at the age of 10 . He continue
 d his music endeavors through high school always keeping his eyes on his go
 al of being a professional musician \, most notably to play jazz music. In 
 1974after graduating from Patrick Henry High School in Roanoke Va. he moved
  to Boston to attend Berklee College of Music which he graduated in 1979 wi
 th a Bachelors degree in Jazz Performance. During those years he played and
  recorded around the Boston area with Al Cohn\, Buddy Defranco\, Miroslav V
 itous\, Sal Nistico\, Herb Pomoeroy\, various Berklee ensembles and many lo
 cal Boston musicians. He also took a year of from school and traveled with 
 The Tommy Dorsey Orch. After moving to NYC in 1980\, he has been a strong v
 oice of the NYC jazz scene both playing\, recording and traveling extensive
 ly around the world. He has worked with and recorded on over 200 recordings
  with artists including Ted Nash\, Maria Schneider\, Houston Person\, Joe L
 ocke\, Roseanna Vitro\, Ann Hampton Calloway\, Bill Cunliffe\, Ted Rosentha
 l and many more. In the lastfew years Tim has recorded 3 CD projects of his
  own which 2 of them include all of his own compositions and arrangements. 
 In the last 18 years Tim has been on the faculty of New Jersey City Univers
 ity as their jazz drum instructor as well as leading ensembles. Tim has als
 o been a 4 time representative for the U.S. State Department working for th
 e Jazz Ambassador program and working in conjunction with The Kennedy Cente
 r and Lincoln Center. These tours took him on tours concertizing as well as
  teaching in South America\, Eastern Europe and the Balkans\, Turkey\, Cypr
 ess\, Asia\, Russia\, Kazakhstan and Kyrgystan.</span></p><p><b><span>Josh 
 Richman</span></b><span> - </span>Award-winning pianist\, composer\, and ba
 nd-leader\, Joshua Richman received his BA from William Paterson University
  in 2008. In 2010\, he completed his master’s degree studying jazz piano pe
 rformance at The Juilliard School. Joshua has studied jazz with piano legen
 ds such as Mulgrew Miller and Kenny Barron\, and classical piano with Gary 
 Kirkpatrick. He is a two-time<br>winner of the ASCAP Foundation Young Jazz 
 Composer Award. Along with leading the Josh Richman Quintet\, Joshua has be
 en fortunate to have performed with distinguished artists such as Andrea Bo
 celli\, Wynton Marsalis\, Wayne Newton\, Terell Stafford\, Chris Potter\, R
 andy Brecker\, Peter Washington\, Kenny Washington\, Benny Golson\, Joel Fr
 ahm\, Steve Wilson\, Lea Delaria\, John Ellis\, Harry Allen\, Jeremy Pelt\,
  and Eric Alexander. Joshua also was the pianist for Anthony Rapp and Steph
 en Sondheim at the “Sondheim on Sondheim-In Words and Music” event at Willi
 am Paterson University. Although based primarily out of New York City\, he 
 regularly performs both nationally and internationally. Joshua is currently
  a faculty member at Temple University\, where he teaches classes\, private
  lessons\, ensembles\, and conducts master classes.</p><p><b><span>Anthony 
 Perez</span></b><span> - </span>Bassist Anthony Perez started his musical l
 ife in New York where he was born and raised. After moving to Florida and c
 ompleting his Associates in Arts\, he moved back to work on his bachelors d
 egree in jazz studies at The New School for Social Research. There he spent
  valuable time studying with Steve Kirby\, Rodney Whitaker\, Armen Donelian
  and Bobby Sanabria. Since his graduation\, Anthony has spent much time per
 forming in various Tri-state clubs and music venues. He continued his music
  education by completing a masters degree in jazz performance from New Jers
 ey City University. There he studied with seasoned professionals including 
 Andy Eulau\, Edward Joffe\, Joel Weiskopf\, Pete McGuiness and Bill Kirchne
 r. He has recorded and toured with pianist Oscar Perez’s group Nuevo Comien
 zo and has performed with Duffy Jackson\, Wycliffe Gordon\, Phoebe Snow\, D
 oug Wamble and Winard Harper.</p>  <span><br></span><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T115427Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Christmas Jazz Concert & Reception
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
