DESCRIPTION:The clergy leaders of FIVE&nbsp\;Verona&nbsp\;houses of worship
 \, and one in West Orange\, will continue&nbsp\;a long-standing tradition i
 n town by hosting an<span>&nbsp\;</span><strong><b>Interfaith Thanksgiving 
 Service<span>&nbsp\;</span></b></strong>on<span>&nbsp\;</span><strong><b>Su
 nday\, November 20\, 2022&nbsp\;at 5pm</b></strong>.&nbsp\; The service wil
 l be held at&nbsp\;<strong><b>B'nai Shalom West Orange&nbsp\;</b></strong><
 span>located at 300 Pleasant Valley Way (parking entrance on Woodland Avenu
 e).</span><p>The service will include scripture readings from Islamic\, Jew
 ish &amp\; Christian traditions\, as well as music related to Thanksgiving.
 &nbsp\; Attendees are encouraged to<strong><b><span>&nbsp\;</span>bring a n
 on-perishable or toiletry item</b></strong>&nbsp\;to be donated to a local 
 pantry.&nbsp\; For further information\, contact any of the clergy leaders 
 at the<span>&nbsp\;</span><strong><b>participating houses of worship</b></s
 trong>: B'nai Shalom West Orange\, Calvary Lutheran\, Episcopal Church of t
 he Holy Spirit\, First Presbyterian Church of Verona\, Islamic Center of Ve
 rona and Our Lady of the Lake Roman Catholic Church.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T115427Z
