 nd one in West Orange will host an Interfaith Thanksgiving Service. The ser
 vice will include scripture readings from Jewish\, Islamic &amp\; Christian
  traditions\, as well as music related to Thanksgiving with a joint choir f
 rom a few of the congregations. </span>You may also view the service via <s
 trong>the following Zoom link</strong>: <a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/j/
 88269724564?" target="_blank">https://us02web.zoom.us/j/88269724564?</a>. C
 ontact Father Jerry Racioppi (<a href="mailto:rector@holyspiritverona.org">
 rector@holyspiritverona.org</a>) <strong>by Sunday at 2pm</strong> (or one 
 of the other Verona clergy leaders) for the passcode.<p></p><p><i><span>Que
 stions?</span></i><span> <span> </span>Contact any of the clergy leaders at
  the participating houses of worship: the <b>First Congregational Church of
  Verona\, </b>the <b>First Presbyterian Church of Verona</b>\, <b>Our Lady 
 of the Lake Roman Catholic Church</b>\, the<b> Islamic Center of Verona</b>
 <span>\,</span><b> </b>the<b> Episcopal Church of the Holy Spirit</b><span>
  and </span><b>B’nai Shalom West Orange</b><span>.</span></span></p>
